---
// Educational scoring sandbox. No personal health classifications or storage.
const phases = [{ id: 'down', label: 'Sitting down' }, { id: 'up', label: 'Rising up' }];
---
<details class="rounded-soft border border-line bg-sand/40 p-5 sm:p-7" data-srt>
  <summary class="font-display text-2xl text-ink">How does the score work? Play with an example.</summary>
  <p class="mt-4">Each phase starts at five. A support subtracts one point; unsteadiness subtracts another half point in that phase. The two phase scores are added. This is an illustration of scoring, not an invitation to try an unsupported transfer.</p>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Keep stable support available. If getting down or up is uncertain, painful, or affected by a recent operation, work with a qualified professional. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40569873/">Read the published scoring method.</a></p>
  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {phases.map(phase => <fieldset class="rounded-soft border border-line bg-paper p-4">
      <legend class="px-1 font-semibold text-ink">{phase.label}</legend>
      <label class="block text-sm">Supports used
        <select data-support={phase.id} class="mt-2 block min-h-11 w-full rounded border border-line bg-paper p-2 text-ink">
          {[0,1,2,3,4,5].map(n => <option value={n} selected={n === 1}>{n}{n === 5 ? ' or more' : ''}</option>)}
        </select>
      </label>
      <label class="mt-4 flex gap-3 text-sm"><input type="checkbox" data-wobble={phase.id} class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0 accent-clay" />Unsteady in this phase (−0.5)</label>
    </fieldset>)}
  </div>
  <div class="mt-5 rounded-soft bg-ink p-5 text-paper" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    <p class="text-sm">Example score · not a health verdict</p>
    <p class="mt-2 font-display text-4xl"><output data-score>8</output><span class="text-xl"> / 10</span></p>
    <p data-formula class="mt-2 text-sm">4 sitting + 4 rising = 8</p>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Two people with the same number can need very different support. The useful question is what makes everyday movement easier for you.</p>
  <noscript><p class="mt-3">The interactive example needs JavaScript. With one support in each phase and no unsteadiness, the example total is 4 + 4 = 8.</p></noscript>
</details>
<script>
  import { scoreSittingRising } from '../lib/sitting-rising';
  const initSRT = () => document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-srt]').forEach(root => {
    if (root.dataset.bound) return;
    root.dataset.bound = 'true';
    const render = () => {
      const phases = ['down', 'up'].map(phase => ({
        supports: Number(root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-support="${phase}"]`)?.value ?? 1),
        unsteady: root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`[data-wobble="${phase}"]`)?.checked ?? false,
      }));
      const { down, up, total } = scoreSittingRising(phases[0], phases[1]);
      const score = root.querySelector('[data-score]');
      const formula = root.querySelector('[data-formula]');
      if (score) score.textContent = String(total);
      if (formula) formula.textContent = `${down} sitting + ${up} rising = ${total}`;
    };
    root.addEventListener('change', render);
    render();
  });
  initSRT();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initSRT);
</script>
